WEBVTT

00:00:07.875 --> 00:00:09.333
Stop!

00:00:10.458 --> 00:00:12.250
Nabeshin! Nabeshin!

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.292
Hey, it's you again, Old Man Rikdo!

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:16.750
Stop, stop!

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.583
Old Man, why am I being chased?

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.292
It's because I gave my permission

00:00:21.292 --> 00:00:24.333
to turn Excel Saga into a detective show!

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.750
I see. Now I've solved the puzzle.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.333
Put the two rings together and...

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:30.917
I didn't say all that!

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.500
<i>Sore wa ai ja nai</i>

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.417
<i>Ai wa sore ja nai</i>

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:57.292
<i>Aishite iru kedo aisarete wa inai</i>

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:01.167
<i>Kesshite ai ja nai</i>

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:05.250
<i>Ketsu wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:13.000
<i>Aisaretai keredo motometari wa shinai</i>

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:17.708
<i>Kono mi sasagete inochi nagedashi</i>

00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:21.750
<i>Wakime mo furazu tada hitasura ni</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.667
<i>Damashite sukashite yokohairi</i>

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.875
<i>Tanin o fumitaoshi keri o kamashite</i>

00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:31.042
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:31.042 --> 00:01:32.958
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.833
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:36.750
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.583
<i>Banana no kawa de korondemo</i>

00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:44.708
<i>Sore wa subete ano kata no tame</i>

00:01:44.708 --> 00:01:49.333
<i>Shiite iu nara sore wa kitto</i>

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:57.208
<i>Ai to iu na no chuuseishin</i>

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:11.583
"Merry Christmas"

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:14.375
<i>The season has abruptly become winter.</i>

00:02:14.375 --> 00:02:15.917
<i>Well, never mind that.</i>

00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:17.542
<i>The people, basking in tranquil happiness</i>

00:02:17.542 --> 00:02:20.583
<i>and living peacefully, have not noticed.</i>

00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.917
<i>This town is being targeted.</i>

00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:28.750
<i>If I say it's being targeted,</i>
<i>it's being targeted!</i>

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.167
<i>I confirmed it on</i>
<i>the phone, so I know.</i>

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.667
<i>It's dangerous, perilous,</i>
<i>an emergency, it's bad!</i>

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.125
<i>It's “Oh, my god</i>!”

00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:37.625
<i>What to do? What to do? What to do?</i>

00:02:37.625 --> 00:02:41.583
<i>What would you do?</i>
<i>You let us take care of it!</i>

00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:44.500
<i>That's why I drafted beautiful,</i>
<i>young, fresh warriors,</i>

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.667
<i>who would gladly give up</i>
<i>their lives for the sake of justice.</i>

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:52.458
<i>But they are still inexperienced</i>
<i>as warriors of light!</i>

00:02:52.458 --> 00:02:55.125
<i>There is only one</i>
<i>course of action to take.</i>

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:57.333
<i>That's right, only one...</i>

00:02:57.333 --> 00:03:00.667
My friends, wouldn't
you like to do some work?

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:00.708
We are.

00:03:00.708 --> 00:03:02.083
Oh, that's right.

00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:05.500
Let's back up. Are you enjoying
your current work?

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.000
How could we possibly be enjoying it?
I'm so bored out of my mi--

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.833
We have been given
extremely good work, Sir.

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:19.375
It has wonderful substance,
befitting our salaries,

00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:21.125
and it is enriching.

00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:22.708
Yeah, sure, Matsuya.

00:03:22.708 --> 00:03:24.333
It's easy doing just
the work you're paid to do

00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:27.167
and playing the exemplary civil servant,

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.708
but it's also true that
it's getting pretty boring.

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:34.875
Ah, I see. I have a
proposition for you guys.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.500
I know it's sudden,
but you guys will be going

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.917
to study and train at a branch
office of the prefectural police.

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:42.667
"It's been decided"

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:49.167
Jingle bell! Jingle bell!
Jingle bell, yay!

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.708
You're very lively from the start today.

00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:54.833
Senior, did something good happen?

00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:57.042
Come on! It's the end of the year!

00:03:57.042 --> 00:03:58.042
--And there's a certain festival
at the end of every year!

00:03:58.042 --> 00:03:59.292
--Oh, Lord Ilpalazzo.
--And there's a certain festival at the end of every year!

00:03:59.292 --> 00:04:01.667
--Oh, Lord Ilpalazzo.
--Today is the joyous Christma--

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.042
Oh, it's a crocodile!

00:04:05.042 --> 00:04:05.833
How should I say this?

00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:09.167
Considering the season, water
events are becoming rather rough.

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:10.750
It is cold water, after all.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.500
What are you in
such high spirits for, Excel?

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.542
How could you allow your
body and soul to be swayed

00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:18.708
by such a worldly,
corrupt, capitalistic custom?

00:04:18.708 --> 00:04:21.583
Please pardon me, Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:25.042
But following any more
of the lines in the original work

00:04:25.042 --> 00:04:28.833
is not morally desirable and
I also don't wish to be scolded,

00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:32.708
so let us quickly move the story along.

00:04:32.708 --> 00:04:36.042
I too had that consideration in mind,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:40.250
so I shall accept your opinion
and make it a harmless scene.

00:04:42.625 --> 00:04:47.250
Now, ladies, I will announce
today's plan of action.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:52.417
About today's conquest
plan number 3333...

00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:53.917
But before that, Excel?

00:04:53.917 --> 00:04:54.750
Yes?

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.292
It is not because today is a special day,

00:04:57.292 --> 00:05:00.208
but I have a wonderful present for you.

00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:01.625
R-Really?!

00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:02.583
My.

00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:03.000
--Crocodile! That crocodile!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
--Turn it into a handbag or a belt or anything you like.
--Crocodile! That crocodile!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:06.583
--I have included the necessary tools.
--Crocodile! That crocodile!

00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:08.042
--I have included the necessary tools.
--Oh, here's a knife!

00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:10.583
"Prefectural Police Branch
Office" "Adjacent Police Box"

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:18.375
We've come from the Department
of City Security to study and train.

00:05:18.375 --> 00:05:21.667
Norikuni Iwata, Misaki Matsuya,
and two others, Sir.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.292
What an insulting introduction.

00:05:23.292 --> 00:05:25.125
"Studying and training at a police box?"

00:05:25.417 --> 00:05:28.750
Go home! I ain't got time to play
games with the public office.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.458
We understand. We will do as you--

00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:32.625
Please don't say that!

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:35.792
I've always admired detectives and stuff!

00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:37.750
Going east and west in pursuit of a case!

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.083
Today, another suspect's
hideout to infiltrate.

00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:42.625
The explosive dick,
setting explosives everywhere!

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:43.917
In other words, me!

00:05:43.917 --> 00:05:45.000
It's over, isn't it?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.833
So you made it, you scientist
who betrayed the organization

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:50.500
because you became infatuated
with our love, Misaki.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.042
The world has been saved.

00:05:52.042 --> 00:05:55.125
At the cost of precious,
useless sacrifices.

00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:57.125
Love and peace!

00:05:57.125 --> 00:05:58.500
Don't just kill me off!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.208
Hey, you're alive!
It's a miracle! Watch out!

00:06:02.042 --> 00:06:03.500
Watanabe!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.333
T-That gun...

00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:08.042
The credits will roll soon,
so don't worry about it!

00:06:08.042 --> 00:06:09.792
What's with his expression?

00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:15.583
You guys are so noisy! Just shut up

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:18.292
for like, a little bit, you know?

00:06:18.292 --> 00:06:19.167
A woman?!

00:06:19.167 --> 00:06:19.958
Marry me!

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:20.667
"That's fast!"

00:06:21.042 --> 00:06:23.333
Kaba-poo already told me everything.

00:06:23.333 --> 00:06:26.292
You're all going to be
my assistants for the day,

00:06:26.292 --> 00:06:28.042
so let's be good friends!

00:06:28.042 --> 00:06:29.833
Okay! I'll be friendly!

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.667
Oh, what a good boy! Here's five points.

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:33.250
Yay, five points!

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.917
When I get a bad feeling,
I'm usually right, you know.

00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:36.917
Sorry.

00:06:36.917 --> 00:06:38.667
--Yay! Yay! Yay! Five points!
--Let's get going.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.083
--Yay! Yay! Yay! Five points!
--Hey, you mugs!

00:06:40.083 --> 00:06:42.792
What's the most important
thing for a detective?

00:06:42.792 --> 00:06:45.375
An unerring ability to judge the situation?

00:06:45.375 --> 00:06:46.375
Money!

00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:46.833
Resources!

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:48.708
"That's necessary for a detective?"

00:06:49.125 --> 00:06:51.000
And one more thing.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.917
I think everyone needs a nickname.

00:06:52.917 --> 00:06:53.875
Resources!

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:55.708
"I don't think so..."

00:06:56.042 --> 00:06:58.708
Come on, Nabe-<i>chan</i>, got a case?

00:06:58.708 --> 00:07:01.000
Boss, there's been a
murder on Block Three in Yaoi.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.667
That was good!

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:05.292
Next, Gan-<i>chan</i>, come on over!

00:07:06.042 --> 00:07:08.500
The case isn't happening at the site!

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.292
It's happening in the conference room!

00:07:10.292 --> 00:07:12.417
Even Maxi's bowled over!
Somebody tonight!

00:07:12.417 --> 00:07:14.792
Next, Sumi-<i>chan</i>, you got any cases?

00:07:19.542 --> 00:07:22.875
I like your silence.
Dragon Kurata is Jeet Kun Do!

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:25.833
Next, Matchan,
do it nice and sober. Go, go!

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:28.875
Well, I found out who the perpetrator is.

00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:31.708
Very cute and Xylish!

00:07:31.708 --> 00:07:33.583
You all act like detectives!

00:07:33.583 --> 00:07:35.250
Ooh! We're already detectives?!

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.792
In one word, it's ta-lent!

00:07:37.792 --> 00:07:39.542
It's work, it's work.

00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:41.250
"Patience, patience."

00:07:42.292 --> 00:07:45.458
What kind of idiocy is this?!
Let's go, you squirts!

00:07:47.917 --> 00:07:49.792
Given the choices, this is much better!

00:07:49.792 --> 00:07:52.667
"Christmas & Millen"
"Sale in progress"

00:07:52.917 --> 00:07:55.250
Reptiles are hard to skin.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.583
"X-mas Cake" "Buy it fast!"   "Chocolate Cake"

00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:58.750
Still stinks, just like you'd expect.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.750
Those guys have a lot of
power to close their jaws with,

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.500
but they're wimpy when
they're opening their jaws.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.250
So, you pin their jaws together
and stick a knife in their hindbrain.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.792
Hey, are you listening, Hatchan?

00:08:07.792 --> 00:08:08.292
--Excuse me.

00:08:08.292 --> 00:08:09.042
--Yes, Ma'am?
--Excuse me.

00:08:09.042 --> 00:08:10.458
--Yes, Ma'am?
--I'd like one of these.

00:08:10.458 --> 00:08:10.833
--Mommy, it's Mr. Reindeer.

00:08:10.833 --> 00:08:12.292
--That'll be 1,500 yen. Thank you very much.
--Mommy, it's Mr. Reindeer.

00:08:12.292 --> 00:08:13.958
--That'll be 1,500 yen. Thank you very much.
--That's right, it's Mr. Reindeer.

00:08:13.958 --> 00:08:17.833
Mr. Reindeer's nose is red,
but his head is red too.

00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:22.292
Hatchan! It's soaking,
it's soaking through! The red stuff!

00:08:22.292 --> 00:08:23.833
Oh, your change!

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:25.125
Quit playing around, part-timer!

00:08:25.125 --> 00:08:26.500
Yes, Sir, Boss!

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.125
What happened to the reindeer?

00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:29.625
Huh?

00:08:29.625 --> 00:08:30.458
--Is this her?

00:08:30.458 --> 00:08:34.042
--I can't quite figure out if this street corpse is cute or creepy.
--Is this her?

00:08:34.042 --> 00:08:35.792
Oh, this is definitely...

00:08:35.792 --> 00:08:37.042
Something like that.

00:08:37.042 --> 00:08:38.208
Raise her legs up.

00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:40.208
Careful, careful.

00:08:42.083 --> 00:08:45.208
"Bereavement Room"

00:08:45.292 --> 00:08:48.417
It was just way too late.

00:08:48.417 --> 00:08:50.500
Doctor, there is someone here
who says she is the patient's...

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.417
No, the corpse's friend.

00:08:53.417 --> 00:08:54.708
Let them in.

00:08:54.708 --> 00:08:55.792
Please...

00:08:55.792 --> 00:08:59.958
Hey, there you are, Hatchan!
Really, you can be so troublesome.

00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:00.250
--Hatchan!

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.625
--I am sorry for your loss.
--Hatchan!

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:06.083
We did all we could, but she was
already as dead as they come.

00:09:06.083 --> 00:09:07.750
It is positively not my fault--

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.083
Shut your mouth.

00:09:09.083 --> 00:09:11.375
Oh, okay, I sort of understand.

00:09:11.375 --> 00:09:13.167
I guess she doesn't want to accept it.

00:09:13.167 --> 00:09:15.000
I will say this bluntly.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.833
--She had already breathed her last...

00:09:15.833 --> 00:09:17.417
--Wake up.
--She had already breathed her last...

00:09:17.417 --> 00:09:19.958
Oh, Senior, good morning.

00:09:19.958 --> 00:09:21.167
Come on, let's go home.

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.500
Okay.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.833
Well, thanks for your trouble!

00:09:26.833 --> 00:09:27.167
--No!
--She was definitely dead! Dead! Dead! Dead! Dead!

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:29.792
--What in the world is going on?!
--She was definitely dead! Dead! Dead! Dead! Dead!

00:09:29.792 --> 00:09:32.167
--If you keep punching holes in the definition of death,
--She was definitely dead! Dead! Dead! Dead! Dead!

00:09:32.167 --> 00:09:34.833
--you're going to get dissected
for real one of these days!

00:09:40.375 --> 00:09:43.875
How could this be?
I can't find a single clue.

00:09:43.875 --> 00:09:45.333
"It ain't even been ten minutes."

00:09:45.583 --> 00:09:49.833
Not that I care, but what kind
of case are you pursuing?

00:09:49.833 --> 00:09:51.208
Call me Purin-<i>chan</i>.

00:09:51.208 --> 00:09:52.875
Tell us, Purin-<i>chan</i>.

00:09:55.042 --> 00:09:57.375
It's a pair who committed
burglary and murder.

00:09:57.375 --> 00:09:59.708
I've been chasing them
for forty years already.

00:09:59.708 --> 00:10:02.042
You look pretty young
for forty, Purin-<i>chan</i>.

00:10:02.042 --> 00:10:03.958
"The statute of limitations
has already expired!"

00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:06.958
Hello? Todo here.

00:10:06.958 --> 00:10:10.292
What?! A pair of burglars
broke into a post office,

00:10:10.292 --> 00:10:12.792
took a hostage and ran?!

00:10:12.792 --> 00:10:14.917
It's a case! Awesome!

00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:17.917
Give me the details.

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:21.417
So when you're going to die
in the street, give me a heads-up...

00:10:21.417 --> 00:10:22.667
Hey, Hatchan?!

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:23.875
She's not here again!

00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:25.083
Where did I drop her?!

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:26.250
Burglars!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.250
--How alarming!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.417
--And they've also taken a hostage!
--How alarming!

00:10:29.417 --> 00:10:30.833
Really?

00:10:34.875 --> 00:10:37.208
Hatchan!

00:10:37.208 --> 00:10:40.250
It's them! This MO, it has to be them.

00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:42.167
"But it's just a normal burglary."

00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:45.542
So where are the suspects headed?

00:10:45.542 --> 00:10:48.083
Purin doesn't know!

00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:50.417
Now's not the time for jokes like that!

00:10:50.417 --> 00:10:51.833
I know! It's that way!

00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:53.167
Shuddup!

00:10:55.125 --> 00:10:57.292
<i>Run! Run, run!</i>

00:10:57.292 --> 00:11:00.292
<i>Believe in yourself</i>
<i>and run with all your might.</i>

00:11:01.292 --> 00:11:03.792
<i>What could that be? I can see a light.</i>

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:05.042
Take that! You're in my way!

00:11:05.042 --> 00:11:08.083
Like the “Realm of the Gods”
from that thing!

00:11:08.083 --> 00:11:11.542
But in either case,
if they get out in the open,

00:11:11.542 --> 00:11:13.792
I don't think I will
ever catch up with them!

00:11:13.792 --> 00:11:16.625
At times like this, well... I know!

00:11:16.625 --> 00:11:17.875
Dog whistle!

00:11:17.875 --> 00:11:19.208
Menchi!

00:11:23.333 --> 00:11:27.500
No! Calling one dog isn't
going to help this situation!

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.417
Calm down, me! What I need
to call at a time like this is...

00:11:30.417 --> 00:11:31.875
A horse!

00:11:31.875 --> 00:11:33.500
Come here!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.917
"There is no such
character in the anime series"

00:11:36.167 --> 00:11:38.792
Well, that's enough
of relying on beasts, so...

00:11:38.792 --> 00:11:41.833
Help, Great Will of the Macrocosm!

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:45.500
Mr. Pe!

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.708
No! Pudding! No!

00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:53.417
That's what happens to anyone
who crosses me, even God.

00:11:53.417 --> 00:11:56.708
Being the Macrocosm,
you understand, right?

00:11:56.708 --> 00:12:01.375
Nothing response whatsoever!

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.708
Hatchan...

00:12:04.708 --> 00:12:07.750
Director, was my
heartrending sorrow act okay?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.375
It was good!

00:12:18.375 --> 00:12:19.708
Where are the suspects headed?

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:21.417
According to the call from the police,

00:12:21.417 --> 00:12:23.792
they're going towards
Block Three in Yaoi.

00:12:23.792 --> 00:12:25.917
This is no time
for approximations!

00:12:25.917 --> 00:12:27.667
You've been watching
too many detective dramas.

00:12:27.667 --> 00:12:28.625
"Yeah."

00:12:28.833 --> 00:12:30.917
In any case, all we have
to do is follow the script

00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:33.167
and head for that mountain, right?

00:12:35.042 --> 00:12:40.208
Er... Exactly what
kind of people are you?

00:12:40.208 --> 00:12:41.333
Say, Bro?

00:12:41.333 --> 00:12:42.292
What is it?

00:12:42.292 --> 00:12:42.875
--Can I ask you something?

00:12:42.875 --> 00:12:43.833
--Hey...
--Can I ask you something?

00:12:43.833 --> 00:12:44.708
Sure.

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:47.208
Was there any point in
taking a hostage?

00:12:47.208 --> 00:12:49.250
It's not like we were
surrounded by the police

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.875
or that anyone had a weapon--

00:12:51.875 --> 00:12:54.792
Wrong! You don't get it at all!

00:12:54.792 --> 00:12:57.583
I told you that we don't
do anything halfway!

00:12:57.583 --> 00:13:00.542
Listen to me!
We're burglars, right?!

00:13:00.542 --> 00:13:05.667
Unlike thieves, burglars
barge in to get money.

00:13:05.667 --> 00:13:08.667
If you barge in, you get reported
to the authorities for sure.

00:13:08.667 --> 00:13:10.250
When you get reported,
what do you do?!

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:10.417
--Run!

00:13:10.417 --> 00:13:10.958
--My senior coworker is waiting for me, so...
--Run!

00:13:10.958 --> 00:13:13.042
--That's right! We run! In other words, we're fugitives!
--My senior coworker is waiting for me, so...

00:13:13.042 --> 00:13:15.917
Hostages are a must for fugitives!

00:13:15.917 --> 00:13:16.958
--Soy sauce for sashimi,
ketchup for rice omelets,

00:13:16.958 --> 00:13:19.417
--Are you watching where you're going?
--Soy sauce for sashimi, ketchup for rice omelets,

00:13:19.417 --> 00:13:21.083
and sauce for Japanese pizza.

00:13:21.083 --> 00:13:23.958
Hostages for fugitives.
This is an aesthetic of crime!

00:13:23.958 --> 00:13:26.417
Anyone who forgets about
aesthetics is just an animal!

00:13:26.417 --> 00:13:28.250
We're criminals, right?!

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:28.750
Well...

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.750
Do you want to become an animal
who has forgotten about aesthetics?!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:33.167
Well?! Well?!

00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:36.750
Bro, I think I was wrong.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.542
So you understand, Little Brother?!

00:13:38.542 --> 00:13:40.167
Bro!

00:13:40.167 --> 00:13:41.917
Excuse me.

00:13:41.917 --> 00:13:43.208
What is it?

00:13:43.208 --> 00:13:46.625
Would it be all right if
I opened the window a little?

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:48.625
I am not feeling well...

00:13:50.292 --> 00:13:54.125
B-Bro, she <i>really </i>doesn't look good!

00:13:54.125 --> 00:13:56.417
Oh, sure, opening a window can't hurt.

00:13:56.417 --> 00:13:58.417
He said it's okay, hurry up and open it!

00:14:02.125 --> 00:14:04.292
S-She went back to normal!

00:14:04.292 --> 00:14:05.792
I wonder if it's some kind of disease?

00:14:05.792 --> 00:14:07.792
I-It's not contagious, is it?

00:14:07.792 --> 00:14:10.125
What might you be talking about?

00:14:12.125 --> 00:14:19.125
♪ Blue sky, white clouds, clean air. ♪

00:14:19.125 --> 00:14:21.292
♪ Mountain roads are so unfair. ♪

00:14:21.292 --> 00:14:23.208
♪ Even if you ran with all your might, ♪

00:14:23.208 --> 00:14:25.750
♪ there's no way a
human could catch up to a car. ♪

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.292
This is no time to be singing!

00:14:27.292 --> 00:14:30.417
Who knows what's happening to
Hatchan, even as I speak?!

00:14:30.417 --> 00:14:34.000
Senior, I will be going on ahead.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.042
Oh, maybe she's
been strangled or stabbed

00:14:36.042 --> 00:14:38.708
or simply, flatly,
dug and completely buried!

00:14:38.708 --> 00:14:41.167
Without air and packed into the ground,

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:44.333
I bet even Hatchan
would stay dead, probably.

00:14:44.333 --> 00:14:45.958
This is...

00:14:45.958 --> 00:14:47.917
That's my Hatchan! Good going!

00:14:47.917 --> 00:14:50.333
She left me such
an easy trail to follow!

00:14:50.333 --> 00:14:52.792
I better go after her before it evaporates!

00:14:52.792 --> 00:14:54.125
Hatchan, wait for me!

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:56.542
I'll save you now! I'll save
you right away! I'll save ya quick!

00:14:56.542 --> 00:14:59.833
I feel like I said something
like this before. But that's okay!

00:15:01.125 --> 00:15:03.250
What's this?! What's that?!

00:15:04.292 --> 00:15:05.792
Birds?!

00:15:06.792 --> 00:15:12.333
Let's see, I'm pretty
sure the trail went this way.

00:15:13.333 --> 00:15:16.292
A mountain of birds!

00:15:16.292 --> 00:15:20.375
It's super-easy to follow,
but did Hatchan do this knowingly?!

00:15:20.375 --> 00:15:22.125
No way, right?!

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:29.208
Damn it, I'm going to do this!
I'm going to corner them for sure!

00:15:29.208 --> 00:15:32.042
I won't be able to
rest in peace until then!

00:15:33.042 --> 00:15:35.042
Not until I catch those criminals.

00:15:35.042 --> 00:15:38.292
Why are you so obsessed
with these criminals?

00:15:40.208 --> 00:15:42.958
This hat used to belong to my father.

00:15:42.958 --> 00:15:45.583
Oh, I get it! When you put that hat on,

00:15:45.583 --> 00:15:47.708
your dead father's spirit possesses you,

00:15:47.708 --> 00:15:50.750
and you turn into Super Purin!

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.375
Yeah, right!

00:15:52.375 --> 00:15:53.500
That's exactly right.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:54.583
What?!

00:15:54.583 --> 00:15:56.250
Got it in one!

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.500
Maybe the detective spirit
has possessed me too.

00:15:58.500 --> 00:15:59.583
"It's just a miracle!"

00:15:59.583 --> 00:16:03.750
My father really wanted to
capture those burglars.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:07.500
Even after my mother
got fed up and left us.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:10.750
Even after he died and possessed me.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:15.250
I... I want to grant my father's wish.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:16.625
How admirable.

00:16:16.625 --> 00:16:17.667
Yeah.

00:16:17.667 --> 00:16:19.917
So that's why you're
still chasing the criminals,

00:16:19.917 --> 00:16:21.667
even after the statute
of limitations has expired.

00:16:21.667 --> 00:16:22.917
"What a pain!"

00:16:22.917 --> 00:16:25.708
I know. I know, but...

00:16:25.708 --> 00:16:27.000
Let's go, you pansies.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.958
Yes, Sir, Boss!

00:16:29.083 --> 00:16:30.583
"You guys are too simpleminded."

00:16:30.958 --> 00:16:34.000
We did it, Bro! We're filthy rich!

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.083
No!

00:16:35.083 --> 00:16:36.583
They're all thousand-yen bills,

00:16:36.583 --> 00:16:39.000
and on top of that, they're
all fake except the outside!

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.292
What?! What is this?!

00:16:41.292 --> 00:16:43.792
All together, there's only
twenty-three thousand yen here!

00:16:43.792 --> 00:16:47.667
So in other words, was it a failure?

00:16:47.667 --> 00:16:48.792
You bitch!

00:16:48.792 --> 00:16:50.583
You don't realize at all
that you're a hostage, do you?!

00:16:50.583 --> 00:16:52.292
--Want me to stick my eye down your ear
--Bro, please calm down!

00:16:52.292 --> 00:16:54.083
--and give your duodenum an attitude?!
--Bro, please calm down!

00:16:54.083 --> 00:16:58.792
You shouldn't commit violence
against an unresisting girl, Bro!

00:16:58.792 --> 00:17:02.458
So what about violent words?!
What about violent words?!

00:17:02.458 --> 00:17:05.042
Committing burglary
is enough crime for me!

00:17:05.042 --> 00:17:07.292
Oh, I didn't realize until now,

00:17:07.292 --> 00:17:10.500
but you two committed a burglary then?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.042
Yes, that's right!
We're burglar brothers!

00:17:13.042 --> 00:17:15.292
Though with just 23,000 yen,
it's a little embarrassing to say that!

00:17:15.292 --> 00:17:16.083
Sorry!

00:17:16.083 --> 00:17:17.875
Bro, get a hold of yourself!

00:17:17.875 --> 00:17:19.375
Shut up!

00:17:23.833 --> 00:17:26.375
See what you've done?!
She fell over, poor thing.

00:17:26.375 --> 00:17:28.583
Remember what Auntie
from Noma used to say?

00:17:28.583 --> 00:17:30.500
That we shouldn't raise a
hand against women and children.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.167
W-Was it my fault?! I was at fault?!

00:17:34.167 --> 00:17:35.833
All right, sorry! See?! Not enough?

00:17:35.833 --> 00:17:38.625
--Sorry about that. I'll get you up right away.
--Kneel? Want me to kneel?! Want me to pay damages?!

00:17:38.625 --> 00:17:40.833
Bro, she's not breathing!

00:17:46.458 --> 00:17:48.125
Y-You're right.

00:17:49.125 --> 00:17:50.875
I've never seen one.

00:17:50.875 --> 00:17:54.042
A person... I've... Murderer...

00:17:54.042 --> 00:17:56.750
I've become the kid brother of a murderer!

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:58.417
It's my crime alone?!

00:17:58.417 --> 00:18:01.708
Anyway, we've got to take care
of it, for our future's sake!

00:18:01.708 --> 00:18:04.292
You mean your future, right, Bro?!

00:18:05.208 --> 00:18:07.167
The end of the tragedy.

00:18:07.167 --> 00:18:10.542
Since it's been cut off,
Hatchan must be close by...

00:18:10.542 --> 00:18:12.500
I smell something burning.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.542
Smoke?

00:18:13.542 --> 00:18:15.042
Hatchan!

00:18:16.125 --> 00:18:17.500
Boss, look at that!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.583
It's them!

00:18:18.583 --> 00:18:19.875
Is that a detective's intuition?

00:18:19.875 --> 00:18:21.625
"Probably just random."

00:18:24.542 --> 00:18:28.083
It's burning nice and warm there.

00:18:28.083 --> 00:18:29.917
Oh, there's a bird here too.

00:18:29.917 --> 00:18:32.250
That means Hatchan's in there?!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.792
Goodness! They burned her instead
of burying her! How foolproof!

00:18:34.792 --> 00:18:38.125
Very admirable. But this is no
time to be saying that!

00:18:38.125 --> 00:18:39.750
Hatchan, I'm coming!

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.083
Hatchan!

00:18:41.083 --> 00:18:42.250
Hatchan!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.083
Hatchan!

00:18:44.083 --> 00:18:44.667
--Senio...

00:18:44.667 --> 00:18:47.458
--Charge! Hatchan! It's hot!
--Senio...

00:18:47.458 --> 00:18:50.625
I'm burning, I'm burning!
Roasting barbeque!

00:18:50.625 --> 00:18:51.458
--This way.

00:18:51.458 --> 00:18:52.667
--Yes, Boss!
--This way.

00:18:52.667 --> 00:18:54.667
You're lost, aren't you?

00:18:55.875 --> 00:18:56.917
"It's no jokin' matter."

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.417
Senior...

00:19:00.417 --> 00:19:04.250
Daruma! Daruma! Covered
in flames! Daruma! Daruma!

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.583
My legs came out,
but my arms won't come out!

00:19:06.583 --> 00:19:07.667
I'm out!

00:19:07.667 --> 00:19:09.167
My, Senior.

00:19:09.167 --> 00:19:11.042
Hatchan, what are you doing here

00:19:11.042 --> 00:19:12.958
like this has nothing to do with you?

00:19:12.958 --> 00:19:16.833
Oh, no. I was definitely in
there until just a minute ago.

00:19:16.833 --> 00:19:21.708
It was rather smoky, and I seem
to have wandered out this way.

00:19:21.708 --> 00:19:24.375
And before I knew it,
you were in front of me.

00:19:24.375 --> 00:19:25.792
What about the burglar people?

00:19:25.792 --> 00:19:27.958
Perhaps they got away?

00:19:29.292 --> 00:19:32.667
What was all that
hardship on death road for?!

00:19:32.667 --> 00:19:35.958
You must have noticed my trail,
just as I thought you would.

00:19:35.958 --> 00:19:38.125
I've got a mountain, a valley, a river,

00:19:38.125 --> 00:19:41.542
and an ocean of questions about that,
but anyway, let's go home.

00:19:41.542 --> 00:19:45.125
I'm really tired and I thought
I'd burn out in more ways than one.

00:19:45.125 --> 00:19:47.125
It seems that the case has been settled.

00:19:47.125 --> 00:19:49.708
Shall we go down the
mountain road and hitchhike?

00:19:49.708 --> 00:19:51.208
Yes, Senior.

00:19:51.958 --> 00:19:54.458
You're terrible, Bro! You burned her!

00:19:54.458 --> 00:19:57.250
I was destroying evidence!
Or we'd be destroyed too!

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:58.458
From ancient times, in this country,

00:19:58.458 --> 00:20:01.125
those who passed on
have always been cremated!

00:20:01.125 --> 00:20:03.125
Forget about her!
Give everything back to the heavens

00:20:03.125 --> 00:20:04.375
and let's go somewhere far away.

00:20:04.375 --> 00:20:07.167
If the two of us work together,
we could make it anywhere...

00:20:07.167 --> 00:20:10.417
Burglary, and we took a hostage
and committed manslaughter.

00:20:10.417 --> 00:20:15.167
And now, abandonment and
desecration of a corpse too, Bro!

00:20:15.167 --> 00:20:16.708
Oh, and arson too.

00:20:16.708 --> 00:20:19.292
So this is all <i>my </i>fault?!

00:20:29.667 --> 00:20:32.042
Bro!

00:20:33.167 --> 00:20:34.500
A car?!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.000
Little Brother!

00:20:41.167 --> 00:20:42.375
Everyone, are you alive?

00:20:42.375 --> 00:20:43.375
Just barely.

00:20:43.375 --> 00:20:44.542
"But he's seriously injured."

00:20:44.792 --> 00:20:46.125
Look!

00:20:47.375 --> 00:20:49.583
They're the burglary suspects,
no matter how you look at it.

00:20:49.583 --> 00:20:51.625
The way they look,
they can't explain it away.

00:20:51.625 --> 00:20:54.167
These are the ones my father...

00:20:54.167 --> 00:20:56.333
The ones my father was chasing...

00:20:56.333 --> 00:20:59.625
Father, I did it. I did it.

00:21:01.208 --> 00:21:02.542
You...

00:21:02.958 --> 00:21:04.750
This was your heart's desire, right?

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:08.042
Take them in yourself
and then rest in peace.

00:21:09.042 --> 00:21:10.542
Merry Christmas.

00:21:10.542 --> 00:21:13.208
Brat, trying to act cool...

00:21:13.208 --> 00:21:14.542
Thanks.

00:21:15.208 --> 00:21:17.542
Hideyuki Kuroda, Yosuke Kurata,

00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:19.667
you're under arrest for
the burglary forty years ago

00:21:19.667 --> 00:21:22.958
and the burglary of the post office.

00:21:23.958 --> 00:21:24.500
What's wrong?

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:25.667
"Hurry up and arrest them."

00:21:26.083 --> 00:21:26.917
--It's not them!

00:21:26.917 --> 00:21:28.417
--What?!
--It's not them!

00:21:32.458 --> 00:21:34.667
It looks like there's still a long way

00:21:34.667 --> 00:21:36.708
until you can rest in peace.

00:21:40.042 --> 00:21:42.667
<i>I can't wait. Send the</i>
<i>inexperienced warriors of light</i>

00:21:42.667 --> 00:21:44.417
<i>to study and train under</i>
<i>a capable detective.</i>

00:21:44.417 --> 00:21:46.583
<i>It was a splendid idea,</i>
<i>if I do say so myself.</i>

00:21:46.583 --> 00:21:49.750
<i>But this doesn't mean they've</i>
<i>become full-fledged warriors.</i>

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:52.458
<i>Please order at least two for delivery.</i>

00:21:52.458 --> 00:21:55.750
<i>However, they must have gone</i>
<i>a step, no two steps</i>

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:59.250
<i>up and down and up again</i>
<i>on the stairs to becoming warriors.</i>

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.458
<i>I have not looked forward to seeing</i>

00:22:01.458 --> 00:22:05.375
<i>the development of young</i>
<i>warriors like this since that day.</i>

00:22:05.375 --> 00:22:07.625
<i>No, that was a failure.</i>

00:22:07.625 --> 00:22:09.625
<i>I won't think of it any more.</i>

00:22:09.625 --> 00:22:11.167
<i>I will believe that</i>
<i>those who await me now</i>

00:22:11.167 --> 00:22:13.958
<i>are the true warriors of light.</i>

00:22:13.958 --> 00:22:16.625
Friends, how were
your studies and training?!

00:22:16.625 --> 00:22:19.167
It was the pits.

00:22:19.167 --> 00:22:20.500
I see.

00:22:50.917 --> 00:22:59.333
<i>I knew, ever since that day</i>

00:22:59.333 --> 00:23:06.750
<i>The reason you had approached me</i>

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:14.833
<i>Tender and soft</i>

00:23:14.833 --> 00:23:23.625
<i>That my body is to your taste</i>

00:23:24.583 --> 00:23:32.375
<i>To your hunger-stricken eyes</i>

00:23:32.375 --> 00:23:40.250
<i>How does my body seem</i>

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:48.125
<i>If you are to eat me, do it in one blow</i>

00:23:48.125 --> 00:23:56.875
<i>So that the meat does not get hard</i>

00:23:59.417 --> 00:24:02.625
The shaky production of Excel Saga
has finally crossed the deadline!

00:24:02.625 --> 00:24:03.875
Are we okay, Director?

00:24:03.875 --> 00:24:04.792
We're okay.

00:24:04.792 --> 00:24:07.542
Are we really okay?
Producer Kitayama was looking a bit bitter.

00:24:07.542 --> 00:24:08.250
--We're okay.

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:10.083
--And Jigoku Gumi was saying they were in danger too!
--We're okay.

00:24:10.083 --> 00:24:10.750
We're okay.

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:12.583
You are so full of confidence!
How inspiring!

00:24:12.583 --> 00:24:14.958
But we aren't going to
have a review episode, are we?

00:24:14.958 --> 00:24:16.542
Why are you saying “Uh...”?

00:24:16.542 --> 00:24:17.417
We're okay.

00:24:17.417 --> 00:24:19.500
The Y2K problem finally
breaks out in the anime world!

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.750
Quack Experimental Anime, Excel Saga!

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.083
Next time: “The New Year's
Year-End Party Hidden Talent Contest”

00:24:23.083 --> 00:24:24.667
Is that this year or next year?

00:24:24.667 --> 00:24:25.250
--We're okay.

00:24:25.250 --> 00:24:28.594
--Just <i>what </i>is okay?! Hey, he ran away!
--We're okay.
